  7. A change to the decompose response schema prevents carrying the obligations derived under the previous schema.
       requirements: completion-08
       code evidence: addressed
         7.1  src/acceptance/requirement/ledger.py#@@ -0,0 +1,301 @@
         7.2  src/acceptance/requirement/obligations.py#@@ -667,11 +760,39 @@ def _resolve_attributions(
       test evidence: unsupported  [tier: static]
         (no mapped test)
         recommended test: Obligations derived under the previous schema are not carried forward after the response schema changes.
           inputs:  Use a two-run scenario with the same task text and the same prior ledger entry, but change only the response schema between runs in a way that would alter the carry key while leaving the requirement text unchanged. The second run must be forced through the code path that computes carry eligibility from the current schema, not through a fresh run with no prior.
           detects: A defective implementation that ignores schema changes when deciding carry-forward, so obligations derived under the previous schema are incorrectly carried forward after the response schema changes.
           full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion schema-change-blocks-carry-forward

